        "original_id": "863ef77c-63ff-564c-80f7-616b1cf5c5db",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Species and Taxa: Eucritta melanolimnetes, Eucritta, stem-tetrapods\n- Films: Creature from the Black Lagoon\n- People: William Alland, Jack Arnold, Richard Carlson, Julia Adams, Richard Denning, Antonio Moreno, Whit Bissell\n- Companies: Universal-International\n- Places and Time Periods: Scotland, Viséan epoch, Carboniferous period\n\nFacts:\n- Eucritta melanolimnetes is an extinct stem-tetrapod species in the extinct genus Eucritta from Scotland.\n- Eucritta melanolimnetes lived during the Viséan epoch of the Carboniferous period.\n- The name Eucritta melanolimnetes means \"the true creature from the black lagoon.\"\n- Creature from the Black Lagoon is a 1954 American black-and-white 3D monster horror film.\n- Universal-International produced Creature from the Black Lagoon.\n- William Alland produced Creature from the Black Lagoon.\n- Jack Arnold directed Creature from the Black Lagoon.\n- Richard Carlson, Julia Adams, Richard Denning, Antonio Moreno, and Whit Bissell starred in Creature from the Black Lagoon.",
